{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityEditingGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistedAssociations","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide walks through the four steps to integrate Swidux: add the package, define your types, wire the store, and connect views."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add the Package","anchor":"Add-the-Package","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Xcode:","type":"text"}]},{"text":" File > Add Package Dependencies, paste ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/Swidux"},{"text":", set ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Up to Next Major"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0.0"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Package.swift:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["dependencies: [","    .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/Swidux\", from: \"1.0.0\"),","]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Define-Your-Types","text":"Define Your Types","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Re-export Swidux from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" so no other file needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["\/\/ App\/AppState.swift","import Foundation","@_exported import Swidux","","@Swidux","struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var items: EntityStore<Item> = .init()","    var tags: EntityStore<Tag> = .init()","    @Slice var ui: UIState = .init()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" requires an explicit type annotation on every stored property — it needs the type at macro-expansion time, and can’t always infer one from the initializer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" generates an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" companion class and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" marks nested state slices that get their own observer class for per-property observation granularity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Specialize the generic effect system with your action type:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ App\/Effect.swift","typealias Send = Swidux.Send<AppAction>","typealias Effect = Swidux.Effect<AppAction>"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void"},{"text":" — dispatched actions hop back to the MainActor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" holds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" async operation and cancellation metadata. Construct it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Effect { send in ... }"},{"type":"text","text":"; the store runs its operation off the MainActor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Define your action tree and root reducer:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ App\/AppAction.swift","enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case items(ItemAction)","    case tags(TagAction)","}","","\/\/ App\/AppReducer.swift","struct AppReducer: SwiduxReducer {","    let itemReducer = ItemReducer()","    let tagReducer  = TagReducer()","","    func reduce(","        state: inout AppState,","        action: AppAction,","        environment: AppEnvironment","    ) -> Effect? {","        switch action {","        case .items(let action):","            return itemReducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","        case .tags(let action):","            return tagReducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Feature reducers conform to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxReducer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"Action = FeatureAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"RootAction = AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Return "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when no async work is needed:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct ItemReducer: SwiduxReducer {","    func reduce(state: inout AppState, action: ItemAction, environment: AppEnvironment) -> Effect? {","        switch action {","        case .increment(let id):","            state.items.modify(id) { $0.count += 1 }","        }","        return nil","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Wire-the-Store","level":2,"text":"Wire the Store"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a generic ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" class that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and observation layer. Define a typealias and a factory method:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["typealias AppStore = Store<AppState, AppAction>","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() -> AppStore {","        let reducer = AppReducer()","        let environment = AppEnvironment.live()","","        let persistencePlugin = PersistencePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","            writers: [","                StateWriter(keyPath: \\.items) { writes, deletes in","                    for item in writes { try await db.upsert(item) }","                    for id in deletes  { try await db.delete(id: id) }","                },","            ]","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","        return Store(","            initialState: AppState(),","            reducer: { state, action in","                reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","            },","            plugins: plugins","        )","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Registering "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plugins"},{"type":"text","text":" is all the wiring it needs — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":" finds it there for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.mutate { … }"},{"text":" and undo\/redo, the two paths that drain outside the plugin lifecycle, so you don’t have to name it a second time as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistencePlugin:"},{"text":". That parameter still exists, for draining through a plugin you deliberately didn’t register.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles the snapshot pattern internally — packing the observer tree into a struct, running the reducer, then unpacking only changed properties back. Views access state through ","type":"text"},{"code":"@dynamicMemberLookup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which forwards to the generated observer class tree.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Wire-Views","type":"heading","text":"Wire Views"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Views read from the store and dispatch actions. They don’t import Swidux or touch the database:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct ItemListView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        List(store.items.values) { item in","            Text(item.name)","        }","        .toolbar {","            Button(\"Add\") { store.send(.items(.create)) }","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"App-Entry-Point","level":3,"text":"App Entry Point"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Own the store with "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and inject it via ","type":"text"},{"code":".environment()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    @State private var store = AppStore.configured()","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(store)","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Learn the full "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" API"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure persistence writers"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","type":"reference"},{"text":" — Understand the snapshot pattern and performance considerations","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Hand-write observation bridging for advanced cases"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"title":"Send","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Sen